body:
@Bromeon 
I wonder why you always bring `default:` to the table. The patch is not adding `default:` to the switch, it's just adding a return _after_ the switch, so that all possible code paths have a return statement (yes, I know, the path is not possible because all cases are handled, but lint tools often do not go that far, and I still think that it even increases readability).

That means you'll still be warned if there's a new case value that's not handled in the switch.
